<section>
    <h2>Three building blocks</h2>
    <div class="card-row">
        <div class="card fragment">
            <h4>HttpClient component</h4>
            <p class="card-tag"><code>RecorderHttpClient</code></p>
            <p>Decorates the HTTP client: replays, records, or passes through.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card violet fragment">
            <h4>PHPUnit Bridge</h4>
            <p class="card-tag"><code>#[UseRecord]</code></p>
            <p>Tells which HAR file a test uses.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card amber fragment">
            <h4>When running the tests</h4>
            <p class="card-tag"><code>SYMFONY_HTTP_RECORDER</code></p>
            <p>Decides whether to replay or to record.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
    <aside class="notes">
        Three pieces. In the HttpClient component, RecorderHttpClient: a decorator that, for each request, replays a recorded response, records the real one, or lets it through. In the PHPUnit Bridge, the UseRecord attribute, which names the file a test uses. And an environment variable, SYMFONY_HTTP_RECORDER, which decides when you launch the tests whether you replay or record. We will look at each of them.
    </aside>
</section>
